1. { -KEY- } Rd1 $1 ( { a) Here Black enjoys some counterplay for the pawn; e.g. } 1. Re7 $6 Rb8 $1 2. Be4 Nc5 ) 
 ( { b) Or } 1. Re2 $6 Rc8 $1 { when } 2. Rd2 $2 { fails to } Rc1 3. Bf1 Ne1 { However, Smyslov finds a much better solution, based on the domination of the enemy knight. } ) 
Nxb2 ( { Of course not } 1... Nxf2 $2 2. Rf1 ) 
2. Rxd4 { The magic distance. From now on, the knight will be badly missed in Black's kingside defence; besides which, the knight itself runs the danger of being trapped. } h6 ( { a) After } 2... Rc8 { both } 3. Be4 Rc1 ( { and } 3... Rc7 4. Rd5 $1 h6 5. Rd6 Kg7 6. Rg6 ) 
4. Kg2 Rd1 5. Rb4 Rd2 6. Kf1 $1 Nd1 7. Rb8 ( { not } 6... h6 6. Ke1 $2 Rb2 $1 ) 
Kg7 8. Rb7 Kf6 9. Ke1 { win for White. } ) 
 ( { b) While } 2... Re8 3. Be4 Nd1 4. Bf5 Rf8 5. Bxh7 $1 Nxf2 6. Bc2 { again leaves the knight decisively dominated; e.g. } Nh3 7. Kg2 Rf2 8. Kxh3 Rxc2 9. Rd5 g4 10. Kxg4 Rxh2 11. Rh5 { etc - Smyslov. } ) 
3. Be4 Rf6 4. f3 Kg7 5. Kg2 $1 { Preparing Kh3-g4-h5 in order to include his majesty in the kingside attack. } Ra6 ( { The restrictive } 5... h5 { now fails to } 6. Rd5 $1 Kh6 7. Rd7 { - Smyslov. } ) 
6. Kh3 Na4 7. Rc4 $1 { The knight is denied c5 and c3. } Nb2 ( 7... Nb6 { would run into } 8. Rc6 ) 
 ( { Again } 7... h5 { wouldn't work, this time due to } 8. Rc7 Kf6 9. Rh7 { winning a pawn - Smyslov. } ) 
8. Rc7+ Kf8 9. Kg4 Nd1 10. Kh5 Ne3 11. Rc3 $1 Nf1 ( { After } 11... Nd1 12. Rc1 Ne3 ( { or } 12... Nf2 13. Bg6 ) 
13. Re1 Nc4 14. Bd3 $1 { Black is lost as well. } ) 
12. Bd3 ( { In view of } 12. Bd3 Ra1 13. Bxf1 Rxf1 14. Kxh6 { Black resigned. } ) 

